      'Kushtha (skin diseases) are the primary indication - require internal cleansing (Shodhana) before external treatment',
      'Oil smearing (Snehana) before application enhances drug penetration through skin channels (Srotas)',
      'Mustard oil (Sarshapa Taila) commonly used as base for external applications due to Tikshna (sharp) property',
      'Ox bile (Gopitta) used as binding agent for enhanced penetration - breaks through skin barriers',
      'Udvartana (powder massage) with buttermilk base for Kapha skin diseases and obesity',
