    topics: [
      { title: '13 Natural Urges by Dosha', content: 'Vata urges (3): flatus (Vata Vega), defecation (Purisha Vega), urination (Mutra Vega). Tridoshic (2): sneezing (Kshavathu), yawning (Jrumbha). Pitta (2): hunger (Kshut), thirst (Trishna). Kapha (2): tears (Ashru), sleep (Nidra). Mixed (4): breathlessness after exertion (Shrama-shvasa - Vata-Pitta), shivering (Trasa - Vata-Kapha), vomiting (Chhardi - Vata-Kapha), seminal urge (Shukra Vega - Vata-Pitta).', clinicalRelevance: 'Classifying urges by dosha helps predict which diseases will arise from their suppression and guides treatment selection.' },
      { title: 'Specific Diseases from Each Suppression', content: 'Flatus: Udavarta, Gulma, Shula, Anaha. Defecation: Udavarta, Shula, Shiroruja, Vibandha. Urination: Shula, Ashmari, Prameha, Mutraghata. Sneezing: Shiroruja, Manyastambha, Ardita, Hikka. Yawning: Shiroruja, Manyastambha. Hunger: Karshya, Shula, Daurbalya. Thirst: Shiroruja, Moha, Daurbalya. Tears: Shiroruja, Netraroga, Moha. Sleep: Tandra, Shiroruja, Angamarda. Breathlessness: Hridroga, Shula, Shiroruja. Shivering: Angamarda, Shopha. Vomiting: Kushtha, Shotha, Pandu, Aruchi. Seminal: Shukrameha, Ashmari, Medra Shula.', clinicalRelevance: 'Each suppression has a predictable disease pattern - knowing this enables targeted treatment.' },
      { title: 'Udavarta - The Core Disease', content: 'Udavarta (upward Vata movement) is the primary consequence of all urge suppressions. When natural downward flow of Apana Vata is obstructed, it reverses direction causing symptoms throughout the body. Symptoms: abdominal distension, pain, constipation, headache, chest pain, difficulty breathing. Treatment: Vatanulomana (restoring downward Vata movement) with Hingvastak churna, Triphala, warm oil massage, and Basti (enema).', clinicalRelevance: 'Many chronic conditions are actually Udavarta in disguise - always assess for urge suppression in unexplained symptoms.' },
      { title: 'Prevention Through Dinacharya', content: 'Proper daily routine prevents urge formation: fixed meal times (regular bowel habits), adequate hydration (prevents thirst suppression), adequate sleep (prevents sleep suppression), proper clothing (prevents shivering), gradual exercise (prevents breathlessness), nasal hygiene (prevents excessive sneezing), emotional management (prevents tear suppression). The key is regularity - irregular lifestyle causes irregular urges.', clinicalRelevance: 'Prevention is always easier than treatment - teaching patients proper Dinacharya prevents Vega Dharana diseases.' },
    ],
    diseaseDescriptions: [
      { name: 'Udavarta (Upward Vata Movement)', sanskrit: 'उदावर्त', etiology: 'Suppression of natural urges (Vega Dharana) - especially flatus, defecation, and urination. Also caused by excessive exercise, fasting, dry food, cold exposure, anxiety, and irregular eating habits. Vata reverses its normal downward (Anuloma) direction and moves upward (Pratiloma).', symptoms: ['Adhmana (abdominal distension)', 'Shula (colic pain - intermittent)', 'Shiroruja (headache)', 'Hridroga (chest pain)', 'Shwasa (difficulty breathing)', 'Vibandha (constipation)', 'Guruta (heaviness)', 'Antra Kujana (borborygmi)'], prognosis: 'Sadhya (curable) when recent and single urge suppression. Yapya (manageable) when chronic. Krichrasadhya when multiple urges suppressed over long period.', treatment: 'Vatanulomana (downward Vata movement): Hingvastak churna, Trikatu, warm oil abdominal massage, Basti (enema) with Dashamula oil. Restore regular urge habits.' },
      { name: 'Ardita (Facial Paralysis)', sanskrit: 'अर्दित', etiology: 'Vitiation of Vata in head region - caused by suppression of sneezing (Kshavathu Vega Dharana), excessive talking, sleeping in improper position, cold exposure to face, head injury. Vata enters facial nerves (Siras) causing paralysis.', symptoms: ['One-sided facial drooping', 'Inability to close eye on affected side', 'Difficulty eating and drinking', 'Slurred speech', 'Drooling of saliva', 'Loss of taste on affected side', 'Pain behind ear', 'Headache on affected side'], prognosis: 'Sadhya (curable) in recent cases (within 1-2 weeks). Krichrasadhya in chronic cases. Better prognosis in young patients.', treatment: 'Nasya (nasal therapy) with Anu Taila or sesame oil. Shiro Abhyanga (head massage) with warm oil. Facial exercises. Internal: Ashwagandha, Bala, Dashamula. Basti for Vata pacification.' },
      { name: 'Ashmari (Urinary Stones)', sanskrit: 'अश्मरी', etiology: 'Suppression of urination (Mutra Vega Dharana) combined with Pitta vitiation and Kapha involvement. Excessive intake of Pitta-aggravating foods, dehydration, sedentary lifestyle. Crystals form in concentrated urine when urination is suppressed.', symptoms: ['Mutra Shula (urinary pain)', 'Mutra Krichrata (difficulty urinating)', 'Rakta Mutra (blood in urine)', 'Mutra Vega (frequent urge)', 'Adhodara Shula (lower abdominal pain)', 'Medra Shula (penile pain)', 'Mutra Sangha (urinary obstruction)', 'Shukra Mutra (semen in urine)'], prognosis: 'Sadhya (curable) when stones are small and recent. Krichrasadhya when large or multiple. Asadhya when associated with severe complications.', treatment: 'Gokshura (Tribulus terrestris), Pashanbheda (Bergenia ligulata), Varuna (Crataeva nurvala) for stone dissolution. Basti with Dashamula oil for Vata pacification. Adequate hydration. Avoid Pitta-aggravating foods.' },
    ],
    treatmentProtocols: [
      { condition: 'Udavarta from Flatus/Defecation Suppression', treatment: 'Vatanulomana (downward Vata movement) with herbs, Basti, and abdominal massage', herbs: ['Hing (Ferula asafoetida)', 'Shunthi (Zingiber officinale)', 'Ajwain (Trachyspermum ammi)', 'Saindhava (rock salt)', 'Triphala (three fruits)', 'Sesame oil', 'Dashamula (ten roots)'], dosage: 'Hingvastak Churna 3g with warm water before meals. Abdominal massage with warm sesame oil 15-20 minutes daily. Basti with Dashamula oil 60ml.', duration: '7-14 days for acute, 28 days for chronic', precautions: ['Restore regular bowel habits immediately', 'Avoid constipating foods', 'Regular meal times', 'Do not suppress any urges during treatment'] },
      { condition: 'Mutraghata from Urinary Suppression', treatment: 'Mutra Virechana (diuretic therapy) + Basti for Vata pacification', herbs: ['Gokshura (Tribulus terrestris)', 'Pashanbheda (Bergenia ligulata)', 'Varuna (Crataeva nurvala)', 'Shunthi (Zingiber officinale)', 'Yavakshara (barley ash)', 'Ghee', 'Warm water'], dosage: 'Gokshura Kwatha 40ml + Yavakshara 1g twice daily. Warm water intake 2-3 liters daily', duration: '7-14 days for acute, 42 days for stones', precautions: ['Monitor urine output', 'If complete obstruction, immediate catheterization needed', 'Avoid Pitta-aggravating foods', 'Adequate hydration essential'] },
      { condition: 'Ardita from Sneezing Suppression', treatment: 'Nasya (nasal therapy) + Shiro Abhyanga + Vatanulomana', herbs: ['Anu Taila (medicated nasal oil)', 'Sesame oil (Tila Taila)', 'Ashwagandha (Withania somnifera)', 'Bala (Sida cordifolia)', 'Dashamula (ten roots)', 'Ghee (Ghrita)'], dosage: 'Nasya: 6-8 drops of Anu Taila in each nostril, twice daily. Shiro Abhyanga: warm sesame oil massage 20-30 minutes daily', duration: '28-42 days continuous treatment', precautions: ['Start treatment early for best results', 'Avoid cold exposure to face', 'Facial exercises alongside treatment', 'Basti for severe cases'] },
    ],
