      'Patient (Rogi) four qualities: Smriti (good memory of symptoms and instructions), Abhirutva (courage and positive attitude), Gyapti (obedience to physician instructions), Satvava (truthfulness about symptoms and habits)',
      'All four components must be present for successful treatment - like a four-legged chair, deficiency in any one leg causes collapse',
      'Physician is the most important component - guides all other components',
      'Treatment success (Chikitsa Siddhi) depends on the integrated functioning of all four components',
      'Deficiency assessment: identify which component is weak and address it before treatment begins',
      'Patient selection: Asadhya (incurable) patients should not be treated - knowing when NOT to treat is as important as knowing how to treat',
