    summary: 'Discusses the three fundamental desires (Trishna) of human life: desire for longevity (Ayu), desire for wealth (Dhan), and desire for fame (Yasha). Emphasizes that health (Arogya) is the foundation for achieving all three desires. Establishes that through proper understanding and application of Ayurvedic principles, all desires can be fulfilled. Highlights the role of Trisutra (Hetu-Linga-Aushadha) knowledge in maintaining health and achieving life goals.',
